messages:
harper: I opened a small PR to add an explicit 'per-request opt-out' example and to recommend a `fallback_flag` field in model cards. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/9981

noor: Could you also show how to prefer a variant for background jobs? Ops keeps asking for a canonical snippet.

harper: added two snippets: one for opt-out and one for preferred-variant. Pasting them below so reviewers can copy: 

```js
// opt-out for a single call
import Redwood from '@redwood/inference'
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.RW_API_KEY })

await client.generate({
  model: 'horizon6b@2026-02-01',
  input: 'Summarize the docs changes',
  routing: { allow_fallback: false }
})
```

```js
// prefer cheaper variant for batch job
await client.generate({
  model: 'horizon6b@2026-02-01',
  input: 'Index daily logs',
  routing: { preferred_fallback: [{model: 'horizon6b-q4', weight: 1.0}] }
})
```

felix: Nice. Please add a note about KV-cache: if you disable fallback for long-context models you should also surface `seq_ceiling` in the model card.

harper: added `seq_ceiling` recommendation in PR and a short YAML example for model-card maintainers. Also linked to the Console doc about routing events.

docs-bot: Running link-check and snippet-lint on PR #9981. Snippet-lint OK. Links OK.

noor: small editorial nit: change `fallback_flag` to `fallback_control` to be less ambiguous.

harper: updated PR to `fallback_control`. merging after docs-bot green and a quick review from eng-ml.

felix: LGTM, thanks. I'll sweep a couple of model cards tomorrow to add `seq_ceiling` where missing.

